Previous Lessons:
1. Always use '=' followed by a single expression when defining function bodies in Alloy 6; using curly braces for function bodies is only valid for predicates and facts, not functions.
2. Curly-brace set comprehensions cannot be used as function bodies in Alloy 6; functions must return a single expression or quantifier expression of the declared type.**
3. [LESSON]: Always verify that all parentheses and curly braces are balanced and properly nested in Alloy functions and predicates, especially when using nested quantifiers or set comprehensions; missing closures can cause Alloy to report confusing syntax errors at seemingly unrelated locations.
4. Can't use parentheses ( ) for function/predicate application in Alloy 6 → Must use brackets [ ] for arguments.
5. Trailing commas after the last field in a signature declaration are not allowed in Alloy 6 and will trigger syntax errors; always ensure the closing brace follows the last field directly.

